  "id": "medullary-sheath",
  "term": "medullary sheath",
  "definition": "The medullary sheath is the covering that may form around a nerve fibre’s axis cylinder after it leaves the nerve cell. In this account, it is one of the nerve’s sheaths and serves mainly to insulate and protect the fibre.",
